<title>BRAZIL: Banco Real Q1 net 50.124 mln reais.</title>
<headline>Banco Real Q1 net 50.124 mln reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian private bank Banco Real issued the following statement on its consolidated results for the January-to-March period.</p>
<p>			    Q1 1997</p>
<p>    Net profit	   50.124 million</p>
<p>    Net worth	     1.652 bln</p>
<p>    Total assets	 17.696 bln</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>The bank said it showed an annualized 13 percent return on equity.  </p>
<p>Rene Aduan, director at Banco Real, said the bank's net profit should not be compared with its 210.2 million real net income a year ago, as last year's first quarter earnings included 190 million reais of revenues from the sale of so-called FCVS debt paper.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
